From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 06:05:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the CPU PMUs

The CPU performance monitors of the A733 are not described, so perf
has no hardware counters and no sampling.

Add one PMU node per core type, so that each gets the event map of its
core: Cortex-A55 on cpu0-5 and Cortex-A76 on cpu6-7, each bound to its
cores through a PPI partition. The overflow interrupt is PPI 7 (INTID
23, "PMU interrupt request" in the user manual's interrupt table). On
the A733 a sampling event raises it only in the column of the core it
runs on, on both core types, and its trigger field in the
redistributor is read-only at level.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the kernel registers
armv8_cortex_a55 for cpus 0-5 and armv8_cortex_a76 for cpus 6-7, each
with 7 counters, both on INTID 23. No events were counted in this test.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 0ce0162f0d14..9cc778a2c00d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -300,6 +300,16 @@ osc: osc-clk {
 		clock-output-names = "hosc";
 	};
 
+	pmu-a55 {
+		compatible = "arm,cortex-a55-pmu";
+		interrupts = <GIC_PPI 7 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH &ppi_partition0>;
+	};
+
+	pmu-a76 {
+		compatible = "arm,cortex-a76-pmu";
+		interrupts = <GIC_PPI 7 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH &ppi_partition1>;
+	};
+
 	psci {
 		compatible = "arm,psci-1.0", "arm,psci-0.2";
 		method = "smc";
@@ -509,6 +519,16 @@ gic: interrupt-controller@3400000 {
 			reg = <0x03400000 0x10000>,
 			      <0x03460000 0x100000>;
 			interrupts = <GIC_PPI 9 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+
+			ppi-partitions {
+				ppi_partition0: interrupt-partition-0 {
+					affinity = <&cpu0 &cpu1 &cpu2 &cpu3 &cpu4 &cpu5>;
+				};
+
+				ppi_partition1: interrupt-partition-1 {
+					affinity = <&cpu6 &cpu7>;
+				};
+			};
 		};
 
 		mmc0: mmc@4020000 {
